userStories.description:
**Goal** — Make prompt-audit records produced by the sessionless complete() path name the stage they ran at in their filename and carry the session id the native adapter already sends to the provider.

**Motivation** — Audit records written by the sessionless complete() path carry a constant complete filename suffix that discards the stage the record's own header knows, and carry no session identity even though that path derives a session id and sends it to the provider; within one session the records are distinguishable only by their millisecond timestamp prefix, and correlate to nothing.

**Approach** — Two independent gaps in one story because both are edits to the prompt-audit record for the same call shape. deriveAuditSuffix (src/runtime/prompt-auditor.ts:145): baseline returns the constant "complete" for a complete entry. Target: returns the entry's stage joined to complete (acceptance-complete) when entry.stage is set, and the bare "complete" when it is not — mirroring the run branch immediately above, which already puts the stage in the name. CompleteResult (src/agents/types.ts:382): add optional sessionId, absent on adapters that do not set it. CompleteDispatchEvent (src/runtime/dispatch-events.ts:83): additionally carries an optional sessionId. It is a plain field rather than the sibling protocolIds object because a one-shot has no record id and no turn id. attachAuditSubscriber (src/runtime/middleware/audit.ts:5): baseline populates sessionId on the audit entry only in the session-turn branch, from event.protocolIds.sessionId. Target: a complete event's sessionId, when present, reaches the audit entry's existing sessionId field. The native adapter's one-shot complete() path already derives nativeSessionId(this.oneShotKey) and sends it to the provider as sessionId (src/agents/native/adapter.ts:180) — it must also return that same value as CompleteResult.sessionId. buildCompleteEvent (src/agents/manager-dispatch.ts) assembles the dispatch event and must carry sessionId through from its input to the returned event.

**Scope** — In: prompt-auditor.ts deriveAuditSuffix, CompleteResult, CompleteDispatchEvent, attachAuditSubscriber, buildCompleteEvent, the native adapter's complete() sessionId plumbing. Out: extending the #1824 per-conversation ordinal to complete records; redaction/rotation/access-control for session ids in the prompt-audit directory.

**Interface**
```typescript
// src/agents/types.ts — CompleteResult gains a field
export interface CompleteResult {
  output: string;
  tokenUsage: TokenUsage;
  estimatedCostUsd: number;
  exactCostUsd?: number;
  sessionId?: string;
  // ...existing fields unchanged
}

// src/runtime/dispatch-events.ts — CompleteDispatchEvent gains a field
export interface CompleteDispatchEvent extends DispatchEventBase {
  readonly kind: "complete";
  readonly sessionId?: string;
}
```

**Goal** — Make buildRateCard report which branch it took (config override vs nax-ai catalog) and have the native adapter's complete() and sendTurn() attach that source to their results.

**Motivation** — First half of #1817: on the native transport the cost figure is computed from nax-ai's real catalog rates while the row is stamped pricingSource: "fallback-rates", which is documented to mean the number came from a generic $3/$15-per-1M card; the value exists so an operator can tell a guessed estimate from a real one, and on this path it fires on estimates that are not guessed.

**Approach** — buildRateCard (src/agents/native/models.ts:209): baseline `buildRateCard(catalog, override) -> TokenPricing`, returning the override wholesale when present and a card built from the catalog otherwise. Target: returns both the card and the branch it took — the rate object plus a source discriminant that is config-override when an override was supplied and catalog-rates otherwise. Its two call sites are src/agents/native/adapter.ts:187 and :224. Why the pricing source is reported rather than re-derived: resolvePricingSource re-states the MODEL_PRICING[bareModel] predicate that the estimator uses, and that duplication is the defect — on the native path the estimator prices from nax-ai's catalog while the label consults a table the catalog was chosen to avoid maintaining. The fix therefore does not add a second predicate anywhere. buildRateCard already owns the single override !== undefined branch that decides which card is used, so it reports the branch it took, and that value travels with the result to the row (US-004 consumes it). Nothing consumes the field yet in this story.

**Scope** — In: buildRateCard's return shape, its two adapter.ts call sites, CompleteResult.pricingSource, TurnResult.pricingSource. Out: wiring pricingSource into dispatch events or cost rows (US-004); honouring tiered pricing (feature-level exclusion).

**Interface**
```typescript
// src/agents/native/models.ts
export function buildRateCard(
  catalog: Pricing,
  override: TokenPricing | undefined
): { rates: TokenPricing; source: "config-override" | "catalog-rates" }

// src/agents/types.ts — CompleteResult gains a field
export interface CompleteResult {
  // ...existing fields (including sessionId from US-002)
  pricingSource?: string;
}

// src/agents/session-types.ts — TurnResult gains a field
export interface TurnResult {
  // ...existing fields
  pricingSource?: string;
}
```

**Goal** — Carry the pricingSource US-003's buildRateCard reports through the dispatch event and have the cost subscriber prefer it over re-deriving from the model string.

**Motivation** — Second half of #1817: the event carries the producer's answer and the cost subscriber prefers it, exactly as it already prefers a wire-exact cost over an estimate on the same line; the ACP path supplies no value and is unaffected.

**Approach** — DispatchEventBase (src/runtime/dispatch-events.ts) target: carries an optional pricingSource, so both event kinds can report the rate card their producer actually used. resolvePricingSource (src/agents/cost/calculate.ts:192): baseline returns "model-rates" | "fallback-rates" | "unknown-model". Target: the same function and the same MODEL_PRICING predicate, with the return union widened to admit "catalog-rates" and "config-override" so producer-supplied values type-check through it. CostEvent.pricingSource (src/runtime/cost-aggregator.ts:70): baseline an inline union "wire" | "model-rates" | "fallback-rates" | "unknown-model", declared independently of resolvePricingSource's return type. Target: the same inline union widened with "catalog-rates" and "config-override" — this is a second, separate declaration site; widening only one of the two leaves the feature half-landed and failing typecheck. attachCostSubscriber (src/runtime/middleware/cost.ts:97): baseline `pricingSource: hasWireExactCost ? "wire" : resolvePricingSource(event.model)`. Target: a wire-exact cost still wins; otherwise a pricingSource carried on the event is used as-is, and resolvePricingSource(event.model) is consulted only when the event carries none — this is the same producer-supplied-wins precedent the "wire" branch on that line already sets.

**Scope** — In: DispatchEventBase, buildCompleteEvent, buildSessionTurnEvent, resolvePricingSource's return type, CostEvent.pricingSource, attachCostSubscriber. Out: honouring tiered pricing (#1843, feature-level exclusion); changing the meaning of existing wire/model-rates/fallback-rates/unknown-model values (feature-level exclusion).

**Interface**
```typescript
// src/runtime/dispatch-events.ts
export interface DispatchEventBase {
  // ...existing fields
  readonly pricingSource?: string;
}

// src/agents/cost/calculate.ts
export function resolvePricingSource(
  model: string | undefined
): "model-rates" | "fallback-rates" | "unknown-model" | "catalog-rates" | "config-override"

// src/runtime/cost-aggregator.ts — CostEvent
readonly pricingSource?: "wire" | "model-rates" | "fallback-rates" | "unknown-model" | "catalog-rates" | "config-override";
```
